{
  "_note": "JSE syntax-completeness wave 1 — lexer + operator grammar (JS-verbatim source forms). Pins: string escape sequences (the JS set; unknown escape = the char itself), template literals (parts string-coerce and concatenate — NOT the numeric-first `+`), // and /* */ comments stripped by the shared source preprocessor (regex literals are never comments — `/\\//g` survives), numeric literals (decimal exponents, 0x/0b/0o radix forms, `_` digit separators), `**` (right-assoc, operands number-coerced ?? 0 like `*`), `??` (nullish = the ONE missing value: null/undefined/NSNull; eager like &&/||), `?.` and `?.[` (pure sugar over the already-total member/index ops), bitwise & | ^ ~ and shifts << >> >>> (JS ToInt32/ToUint32 wrapping), unary +. Statement-level twins (ASI, sugar, comments in bodies) live in the actions corpus.",
